<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<WorkflowBuilder Version="2.9.0"
                 xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                 xmlns:rx="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Reactive;assembly=Bonsai.Core"
                 xmlns:dev="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Devices;assembly=OpenRigs.Devices"
                 xmlns:scr="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions;assembly=Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions"
                 xmlns:orcl="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Control;assembly=OpenRigs.Control"
                 xmlns:lv="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.LiveView;assembly=OpenRigs.LiveView"
                 xmlns="https://bonsai-rx.org/2018/workflow">
  <Workflow>
    <Nodes>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="Binning" DisplayName="Binning" Description="Camera binning, 1 for full resolution, in place of rig.yml's. Stays set for later runs until cleared. Blank: rig.yml's camera binning." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="ConfigRoot" Description="The root under which each machine has its own configuration directory, &lt;ConfigRoot&gt;\&lt;MACHINE-NAME&gt;\rig.yml, read by ReadLabRig (which publishes it to the camera's video writer) and ExperimentRecords (RecordHarpDevices)." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:ReadLabRig.bonsai">
        <ConfigRoot>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs</ConfigRoot>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="SubjectId" />
        <Property Name="SessionId" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Initialization</Name>
        <Description>The experiment controller (OpenRigs.Control, ExperimentControl): SubjectId and SessionId from this node's properties or the command line (--property:SubjectId=...), the run length (whole minutes) and the camera's exposure and gain (CameraExposureUs and CameraGainDb, which Hardware &gt; CameraLiveControls declares and takes live) as parameters the controller may change until Go, and the control endpoint the rig agent talks to (TCP 5561). The workflow starts into ready mode: board connected, camera armed and streaming, nothing recorded, waiting for Go. At Go the IDs and the run length are checked once and published as RunSettings, which logging waits for; if an ID is empty or the run length is not 1 to 9999, the workflow stops with "Sequence contains no elements." and nothing is recorded. Stop from the controller ends the workflow through ExperimentStoppedException, closing every file.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="SubjectId" />
              <Property Name="SessionId" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Control:ExperimentControl.bonsai">
              <SubjectId />
              <SessionId />
              <ControlEndpoint>@tcp://127.0.0.1:5561</ControlEndpoint>
              <Parameters>
                <Parameter>
                  <Name>RunLengthMinutes</Name>
                  <Value>30</Value>
                  <Description>How long to record, in whole minutes (1 to 9999).</Description>
                  <Minimum>1</Minimum>
                  <Maximum>9999</Maximum>
                  <WholeNumber>true</WholeNumber>
                </Parameter>
              </Parameters>
              <Commands />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>SubjectId</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>SessionId</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ParameterValue">
                <orcl:Name>RunLengthMinutes</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Name>RunLengthToInt</scr:Name>
              <scr:Expression>Convert.ToInt32(it)</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
              <Name>RunSettingsValid</Name>
              <Description>Subject and session given, and the run length from 1 to 9999 minutes.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Expression>Item1.Trim().Length &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; Item2.Trim().Length &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; Item3 &gt;= 1 &amp;&amp; Item3 &lt;= 9999</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:First" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>RunSettings</Name>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="9" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="5" To="9" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source3" />
            <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="11" To="12" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="12" To="13" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:LogLabExperiment.bonsai" />
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Hardware</Name>
        <Description>The box's devices: the behaviour boxes' rig list (OpenRigs.Devices BehaviorBoxHardware: ReadyGate, Ready once the board's clock is set and the camera has sent a frame; the Behavior board BehaviorBoard-Main with its own clock and the running wheel on encoder port 2, WheelDistanceCm; the camera Camera-Overhead on the board's camera trigger, Binning, a launch property, in place of rig.yml's while set), each piece from its own entry in rig.yml and logging itself once the experiment folder exists; CameraExposureUs and CameraGainDb taken live by the camera (CameraLiveControls), and the editor's preview (Preview).</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="Binning" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:BehaviorBoxHardware.bonsai" />
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:CameraLiveControls.bonsai">
              <Camera>Camera-Overhead</Camera>
              <Board>BehaviorBoard-Main</Board>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
              <Name>Preview</Name>
              <Description>The editor's preview window (config\main.layout): Value.Image and SampleInterval take 5 images a second from Camera-Overhead.Data, from Start, so it shows the camera in ready mode, and the last three nodes show beside it the exposure and gain the camera reports for its frames (CameraSettings).</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>Camera-Overhead.Data</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>Value.Image</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:SampleInterval">
                      <rx:Interval>PT0.2S</rx:Interval>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>Camera-Overhead.Data</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:SampleInterval">
                      <rx:Interval>PT0.2S</rx:Interval>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Name>CameraSettings</scr:Name>
                    <scr:Description>The exposure and gain the camera reports for its frames (chunk data), 5 a second, for the editor's readout window (config\main.layout): what the camera took, not what was asked for.</scr:Description>
                    <scr:Expression>"Exposure " + Value.ChunkData.ExposureTime.ToString("F0") + " us   Gain " + Value.ChunkData.Gain.ToString("F2") + " dB"</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>TaskLogic</Name>
        <Description>The run: once the experiment folder exists (PathPrefix, which LogLabExperiment makes at Go), RecordVideo counts the run length's frames from Camera-Overhead.Data and completes, and the run reports Finished, which ExperimentManifest records as completed. The board and camera log themselves; ExperimentRecords records the rest.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Camera-Overhead.Data</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
              <Name>RecordVideo</Name>
              <Description>The run: subscribed only once PathPrefix exists (Take reads its Count at subscription), it takes the run length's worth of frames (RunLengthToFrames) and then completes, which reports Finished. The camera piece records the video and its CSV itself, every frame from its first until the workflow stops.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
                    <Name>RunLengthToFrames</Name>
                    <Description>Frames to record: run length (minutes) x 60 x the frequency of the trigger that drives Camera-Overhead, the one whose wiring line in rig.yml names it (OpenRigs.Devices CameraTrigger, as the camera piece finds it).</Description>
                    <Workflow>
                      <Nodes>
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>RunSettings</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>Camera-Overhead</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="dev:CameraTrigger">
                            <dev:MarginMicroseconds>1000</dev:MarginMicroseconds>
                          </Combinator>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                          <scr:Name>RunLengthToFrames</scr:Name>
                          <scr:Expression>Convert.ToInt32(Convert.ToDouble(Item1.Item3) * 60.0 * Item2.Frequency)</scr:Expression>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                      </Nodes>
                      <Edges>
                        <Edge From="1" To="3" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source2" />
                        <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="0" To="5" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source2" />
                        <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
                      </Edges>
                    </Workflow>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="Count" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                    <rx:Count>3000</rx:Count>
                  </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="3" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>PathPrefix</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:SubscribeWhen" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Count" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportPhase">
                <orcl:Phase>Finished</orcl:Phase>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:ExperimentRecords.bonsai">
        <ConfigRoot>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs</ConfigRoot>
        <IngestScript>coen-behaviour-box</IngestScript>
        <ExpectedFiles>auto;harp;Settings/Settings_Rig_;Settings/Settings_Experiment_;BonsaiData/BonsaiData_Async_</ExpectedFiles>
        <TrialColumns />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="lv:StreamDevices">
        <Name>LiveView</Name>
        <Description>Streams every device in this machine's rig.yml that the workflow publishes, over ZeroMQ, for the live view (OpenRigs.LiveView, StreamDevices): data on TCP 5556, video on 5558, on every interface, from Start (in ready mode too). Camera-Overhead.Data as Camera-Overhead.video, 5 JPEG frames a second at 320 x 240; BehaviorBoard-Main.Data as BehaviorBoard-Main.encoder, the raw count from AnalogData, 10 a second; each rate and size can be changed in rig.yml under the device's liveView:. Also elapsed, seconds since the experiment folder (PathPrefix) appeared, once a second, and every 5 s liveview: this workflow, its commit, and the devices streamed and skipped and why. Every message carries RigId, the machine's name, and the session key: "ready" until the experiment folder exists, then its name, sub-&lt;SubjectId&gt;/ses-&lt;SessionId&gt;_&lt;start&gt;. Its ConfigRoot is the lab's, set here and fed by no edge: an edge into it makes Bonsai build it before the devices, so it would stream nothing. Last in the workflow, because it streams only subjects built before it. A port already in use (another workflow streaming) stops the workflow at Start with NetMQ's AddressAlreadyInUseException, before the camera is triggered.</Description>
        <lv:ConfigRoot>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs</lv:ConfigRoot>
        <lv:DataPort>5556</lv:DataPort>
        <lv:VideoPort>5558</lv:VideoPort>
      </Expression>
    </Nodes>
    <Edges>
      <Edge From="0" To="6" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="1" To="8" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
    </Edges>
  </Workflow>
</WorkflowBuilder>
